    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=16020": {
      "title": "University Assistant (postdoc)",
      "description": "University Assistant (postdoc) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (postdoc) Start date/duration: from 20.03.2027 for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Psychology Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Independent research in the field of developmental psychology across the lifespan Independent delivery of teaching modules and conducting examinations Supervising students, including supervising Bachelor thesis Contributing to organisational and administrative tasks as well as evaluation measures Further training Your profile: A completed relevant doctoral or PhD degree in psychology Experience in the acquisition and analysis of brain imaging data and in the use of Matlab, Python, R or SPSS Experience in acquiring and analysing  EEG-fMRI data during sleep in young and older adults is a necessary prerequisite Experience in independently securing third-party funding Very good written and spoken English is also a requirement Experience of working with patient populations is desirable Good communication and collaboration skills, as well as the ability to work effectively in a team Please attach the following documents to your application: A covering letter specifically addressing the job profile, a CV including experience with MRI methods, the publication the applicant considers to be their best work and a brief explanation of why, a list of publications, and two letters of recommendation or the contact details of two referees Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/PSY-SPORT-16020 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#post-doc Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 04.11.2026 stating the code PSY-SPORT-16020 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Univ.-Prof. Dr. Dorothea Hämmerer Phone: +43 512 507 56076 Email: Dorothea.Haemmerer@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
